{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming b9f65395, implementing ratified proposal 6952579a. Every collision I was avoiding is gone: the thread lane merged as 66106cf8, so ui and internal/service carry no candidate of mine, and internal/workroom carries none either since fa99a5fe.\n\nPREMISE CHECKED AT THE ENFORCEMENT SITE, not from the proposal text. internal/workroom/kinds.go:170 still reads starter(KindReport, nil, countKinds(1, 1, KindPromise), ...), so a report is still bound to exactly one promise and this is unimplemented. Proposal 6952579a is live, ratified and not stale; ratification 12ae4b6d is live. I resolved both by substring rather than trusting an eight-character suffix, because these ids abbreviate at either end.\n\nWHAT I WILL BUILD, in the five parts the request names. The report basis becomes exactly one of promise or request. A report whose lifecycle basis is a request is effective only from the request's addressee, and ineffective with a reason naming the promise when the reporter already holds a live promise on that request. The commitment projection treats it as claim-and-complete: performer is the reporter, promise empty, status reported, waiting_on the requester, and ratification by the originating requester or a sealed merge receipt satisfies it. An artifact by the addressee resting on the request with a commit is a completion the same way one on a promise is. Then architecture.md, AGENTS.md and SKILL.md say a promise is optional, spine.ts reads reported-without-a-claim at the promise station, and every new guard gets a test I break to prove it holds.\n\nTWO THINGS I EXPECT TO MATTER AND WILL REPORT EITHER WAY. This changes the fold's admission rules, so it may need the fold profile advanced; I will check rather than assume, and say which. And the running resident is already serving a fold compiled from b97ec09d, so nothing I merge here is in force until somebody rebuilds and restarts -- I will not claim otherwise in the artifact.\n\nOwn branch request/report-rests-on-request and worktree from current main.","body":{"branch":"request/report-rests-on-request"}}